                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"By eleven o'clock, you'll have finished.\" The talk will…",
                        "options": [
                          "be over before eleven",
                          "be in progress at eleven"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"By the time we check in, it'll be dark.\" After by the time we use…",
                        "options": [
                          "the present simple",
                          "will"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Where will Daniel be sitting during the talk?",
                        "options": [
                          "at the back",
                          "in the front row",
                          "next to Lucía"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Future continuous and future perfect",
                    "explanation": "Future continuous (will be + -ing): una acción que estará en curso en un momento del futuro. This time tomorrow, I'll be standing on stage. También sirve para preguntar por planes de forma educada: Will you be sitting in the front row?\n\nFuture perfect (will have + participio): una acción que ya estará terminada antes de un momento del futuro. By eleven o'clock, you'll have finished.\n\nBy + momento = para, antes de (by Friday, by then). By the time + presente = para cuando: By the time we check in, it'll be dark.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Forma",
                        "Uso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "will be + -ing",
                          "en curso en un momento futuro",
                          "This time tomorrow I'll be standing on stage."
                        ],
                        [
                          "will be + -ing (pregunta)",
                          "preguntar por planes con educación",
                          "Will you be sitting in the front row?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "will have + participio",
                          "terminado antes de un momento futuro",
                          "By eleven, you'll have finished."
                        ],
                        [
                          "by + momento",
                          "para, antes de",
                          "by eleven, by Friday, by then"
                        ],
                        [
                          "by the time + presente",
                          "para cuando",
                          "By the time we check in, it'll be dark."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "This time tomorrow, I'll be standing in front of four hundred designers.",
                      "By eleven o'clock, you'll have finished.",
                      "I'll have sent the demo to the organisers by then.",
                      "I'll be sitting at the back, controlling the screen."
                    ]
                  }
